{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Eliphaz answered, ha-nissah</b> — The nun is plural, the samekh stands in place of shin, and the he stands in place of alef. Like it: <i>ha-nissah aleinu or panekha YHWH</i> (Psalms 4:7)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The form ha-nissah (הנסה) is analyzed as ha-nis-sha, i.e. an imperative 'try us,' with samekh replacing shin of the root נסה and he replacing final alef."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:41.553160217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}